sbook><name>SASAKI KUTSUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOZAWA YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHASHI, YUJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RIGAKU CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KUTSUNARI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOZAWA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHASHI YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KUTSUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOZAWA YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHASHI, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KUTSUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOZAWA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A high-speed imaging plate X-ray diffraction apparatus of saved installation space type having an expanded range of 2 theta  measurement angle and a high resolution, and easy to operate. The apparatus comprises an X-ray measuring instrument having an X-ray optical system (5) and a goniometer (1) and adapted for allowing a mounted single crystal sample (3) to diffract X-rays, a cylindrical imaging plate (21) disposed vertically to record X-ray diffracted waves from the sample (3) and covering a range of 2 theta  measurement angle from -60 DEG  to +144 DEG , a drive motor (11) for vertically moving the imaging plate (21), a transmission mechanism (12), a rotary reader (20) disposed coaxially with the moved cylindrical imaging plate (21) and adapted for reading X-ray diffracted wave data on the inner surface of the imaging plate (21).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un appareil grande vitesse de diffraction des rayons X sur plaque imageuse. Cet appareil de faible encombrement, à l'éventail élargi d'angles de mesure 2 theta  et à la résolution élevée, et est d'un emploi facile. L'appareil comprend: un instrument de mesure des rayons X, avec système optique à rayons X (5) et goniomètre (1), qui est conçu pour permettre à un échantillon simple de cristal (3) de diffracter des rayons X; une plaque imageuse cylindrique (21) disposée verticalement qui enregistre les ondes de rayon X diffractées à partir de l'échantillon (3) et couvrant une plage d'angles de mesure 2 theta  comprise entre -60 DEG  et +144 DEG ; un moteur d'entraînement (11) assurant le déplacement vertical de la plaque imageuse (21); un mécanisme de transmission (12); et un lecteur tournant (20) disposé coaxialement par rapport à la plaque imageuse cylindrique (21) et conçu pour lire des données relatives aux ondes de rayon X diffractées sur la surface intérieure de la plaque imageuse (21).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to i